{"id": "EUVD-2025-210858", "enisaUuid": "81a0700a-4e3c-399a-b84a-ba4f86302dcc", "description": "CDT before 1.4.5 contains an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in the opposedVertexInd() function when constraint edge intersections are computed in floating point and round outside adjacent triangles. Attackers can supply nearly-degenerate constraint edges through geometry data to trigger an out-of-bounds array access that crashes the calling process.", "datePublished": "2026-09-05T11:37:59", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T14:17:16", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/artem-ogre/CDT/issues/212", "https://github.com/artem-ogre/CDT/commit/bf0d11ebfe3da0da72aed91816f665aef1b447cc", "https://github.com/artem-ogre/CDT/blob/1.4.4/CDT/include/CDTUtils.hpp#L175", "https://github.com/artem-ogre/CDT/releases/tag/1.4.5", "https://github.com/artem-ogre/CDT", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/cdt-before-1.4.5-out-of-bounds-read-via-opposedvertexind"], "aliases": ["CVE-2025-15647", "GHSA-gg9p-3jmx-h6rw"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.28, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "892cde88-ff60-311a-a88b-af1125b1ede8", "product": {"name": "CDT", "vendor": {"name": "artem-ogre"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.4.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "91b4a7a2-48ae-35b7-94c4-13872b58fd21", "vendor": {"name": "artem-ogre"}}], "isExploited": false}